# A land card is a permanent card with mana value 0 (CR 110.4a, 202.3), so Anticausal Vestige may put one from hand onto the battlefield
# tapped; putting it there is not playing it (CR 305.2a), so the turn's land play is still unused. Bot1 hard-casts the Vestige on turn 1
# (Black Lotus and three Moxen) and on turn 3 exiles it with its own Swords to Plowshares before playing a land: it draws, puts an Island
# from hand onto the battlefield tapped (0 lands controlled, 0 <= 0), and still plays another Island as its land play.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Anticausal Vestige
Swords to Plowshares
Island
Island
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

